@CHARA_INFO_KOJO_K2001_0
CALL CHARA_INFO_HEADER(2001)
PRINTFORML The V32 Horizon debuted in 1989 as either a 2-door coupe or 4-door hardtop sedan.
PRINTFORML It featured several versions of the SJ-series straight-6 engines, which had improved heads, and single-point electronic fuel injection.
PRINTFORML The GDS-t is a 4-door sedan with the turbocharged DOHC 2.0L SJ20DET engine, complete with ABS, a viscous LSD, and four-wheel steering.
PRINTL
PRINTFORML The V32 was considered a "compact" under Japanese legislation that determined the amount of tax liability based on exterior dimensions.
PRINTFORML The smaller engine in the GDS-t provided Japanese buyers cheaper road taxes than the GDS-25 variant.
PRINTFORML Despite this, the GDS-t's SJ20DET had the second highest power output at 212hp (215 PS), only outshined by the GD-X's SJ20DETT with a gentleman's agreement-limited 276hp (280PS).
RETURN 1